  "_fix_note": "M5b / M4 v4 (D-322). Adds route C: the document-chase email DRAFT. M5b cannot be its own scenario (Free plan caps ACTIVE scenarios at 2; M3+M4 are those two), so it rides inside M4. Trigger gains a second OR-group and widens to A1:AE1 so index 30 (AE Chase Flag) is readable at all - without that widening route C silently never fires. Routes A and B gain {{1.`24`}} notexist on EVERY OR-group: without it a CHASE row with a supported visa re-enters route A, refiles the checklist, recopies the file and redrafts the first email. G2 requires Y exist (exact complement of G1) so the three routes partition; proved over 1008 emitted row shapes in verify_blueprints.py. G2 also requires F exist, so rows with no email never enter the scenario at all - they stay flagged CHASE for a human to phone, at zero operations. BOTH exits from the draft clear the flag (DRAFTED on success, 'CHASE DRAFT FAILED - review' on error) or M4 redrafts the same email every run forever. DRAFT ONLY - never ActionSendEmail. Cost: +2 ops per chased row."
